---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/withBase';
---

<LegalLayout title="Payments & Refunds">
  <h1>Payments &amp; refunds</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Summary of clauses 13–16 of the <a href={withBase("terms")}>Terms and Conditions</a>. Last updated: 1 October 2026. If anything here conflicts with the Terms, the Terms prevail.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Currency and sequencing</h2>
    <p>All amounts are in Pakistani Rupees. Payments are by bank transfer to the Khepia account shown in the App. Khepia confirms each payment manually.</p>
    <ol type="1">
      <li>After a match is agreed, the <strong>Sender</strong> pays the full Delivery Fee first (within the time shown in the App).</li>
      <li>Only after that payment is confirmed, the <strong>Passenger</strong> pays the Commission plus the Deposit.</li>
      <li>A Booking is confirmed, and a Tracking ID issued, only after both payments are confirmed.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Delivery Fee (Sender)</h2>
    <p>The Sender offers an amount per kilogram; the App calculates the total from weight. A Passenger may accept or counter-offer. The Delivery Fee is the total the Sender finally accepts.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Commission (Passenger)</h2>
    <p>The Commission is a percentage of the Delivery Fee, at the rate shown in the App when the Booking is made. The rate at the date of the Terms is <strong>10%</strong>. It is payable by the Passenger and is kept by Khepia as its fee for use of the App.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deposit (Passenger)</h2>
    <p>The Deposit equals the Parcel’s Declared Value. Khepia holds it as security for the Passenger’s performance and as the source of any Parcel Protection payment. On Completion it is returned in full with the Delivery Fee, within <strong>5 Working Days</strong> (unless a Problem Report is open).</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How Khepia holds money</h2>
    <p>Khepia receives the Delivery Fee and Deposit into its own account and holds them as stakeholder until Completion, cancellation, or a dispute decision. No interest is paid. Holding these amounts does not create a banking relationship.</p>
    <p>On Completion, Khepia pays the Delivery Fee to the Passenger (to an account or wallet in the Passenger’s own name), returns the Deposit, and keeps the Commission.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Refunds and cancellations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Before a Booking is made, either side may withdraw with no payment involved.</li>
      <li>After payment, cancel through the App or email <a href="mailto:khepia.pk@gmail.com">khepia.pk@gmail.com</a>.</li>
      <li>Refunds of amounts paid are decided case by case (reason, stage reached, and loss to the other User). Deposit returns follow clause 14 of the Terms.</li>
      <li>If a Booking is cancelled before collection (other than for Passenger breach), the Deposit is returned within 5 Working Days.</li>
      <li>If the Passenger refuses the Parcel under the Terms, the Deposit is returned; any Delivery Fee refund is decided case by case.</li>
      <li>Khepia may cancel if payment is missing, a Prohibited Item is suspected, a User is in breach, or the law requires it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Charges and tax</h2>
    <p>Each User bears their own bank and transfer charges. Each User is responsible for any tax on amounts they receive. All Booking payments must go through Khepia as set out in the Terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Full terms</h2>
    <p>See <a href={withBase("terms#clause-13")}>Terms clauses 13–16</a> for the complete payment, deposit, and refund rules.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
